WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.575
- Hi, my name is Jake Watson.

00:00:01.575 --> 00:00:03.646
I'm a co-creative director
of Corridor Digital.

00:00:03.646 --> 00:00:06.309
We're a digital entertainment
studio that specializes

00:00:06.309 --> 00:00:09.085
in narrative video game-inspired content,

00:00:09.085 --> 00:00:10.790
tech experiments, and vlogging.

00:00:10.795 --> 00:00:12.545
- [Carmichael] Are you
practicing while you're going?

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:15.138
- Yeah, I have to do an
intro, and I have to show

00:00:15.138 --> 00:00:17.746
a bunch of these old-timey
guys that I'm actually

00:00:17.746 --> 00:00:19.185
kind of legit.

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:20.923
And I'm also a licensed
entertainment lawyer

00:00:20.923 --> 00:00:23.316
in the state of California.

00:00:23.316 --> 00:00:24.583
I could really button up that ending,

00:00:24.583 --> 00:00:25.929
it's a little too long.

00:00:25.929 --> 00:00:28.596
(soulful music)

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:40.502
- We're here in Salt Lake City.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:41.373
We're gonna go get the car,

00:00:41.569 --> 00:00:43.376
but we gotta make it all
the way up Park City,

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:46.285
it's gonna take two hours
or so, and I don't know.

00:00:46.285 --> 00:00:49.045
I've never been up there, and
I don't know the conditions.

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:52.153
(upbeat music)

00:00:54.018 --> 00:00:54.974
I've never been to a place where

00:00:54.974 --> 00:00:56.709
so many people don't have cars.

00:00:56.709 --> 00:00:58.578
There's probably less
than 1,000 cars in here,

00:00:58.578 --> 00:00:59.780
and we are going to get one.

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:01.897
So, you're like "Oh cool, hey
that's pretty cool, it's got

00:01:01.897 --> 00:01:04.200
a nice backplate and face and everything."

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.897
But wait, check out this.

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:06.420
Oh!

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:09.353
The new Dodge Durango
2015, all-wheel drive.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:10.233
Park City?

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:11.213
- [Attendant] We get a lot of snow there.

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:12.053
- Yeah.

00:01:12.132 --> 00:01:13.263
- [Attendant] Call me if you
guys need anything, okay?

00:01:13.263 --> 00:01:14.096
- [Jake] Cheers.

00:01:14.096 --> 00:01:14.929
- [Attendant] Have a good day, guys.

00:01:14.929 --> 00:01:15.589
- [Carmichael] Thanks.

00:01:16.644 --> 00:01:18.538
- Do you see how nice everyone is here?

00:01:18.538 --> 00:01:19.517
Did you see that guy?

00:01:19.517 --> 00:01:22.210
If more people were like that in L.A.,

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:24.373
it'd be a lot nicer place to live.

00:01:24.373 --> 00:01:25.594
I just got in this car,

00:01:25.594 --> 00:01:27.522
and I've never been in
one of these cars before,

00:01:27.522 --> 00:01:30.605
so I don't know how to open the hood.

00:01:32.381 --> 00:01:34.806
I'm used to driving
motorcycles and old trucks.

00:01:34.806 --> 00:01:39.095
It's a really nice day out
here in beautiful Utah.

00:01:39.095 --> 00:01:40.853
Carmichael and I, we're cruising along,

00:01:40.853 --> 00:01:43.789
heading out of Salt
Lake towards Park City,

00:01:43.789 --> 00:01:45.423
going along the 80, thinking,

00:01:45.423 --> 00:01:47.506
"Oh, it's a couple more
miles until we get to

00:01:47.506 --> 00:01:50.527
"the next freeway that we need to hit."

00:01:50.533 --> 00:01:53.351
We're chatting it up, we're
talking about everything,

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:58.527
and we went 37 minutes in the
wrong direction down the 80.

00:02:00.732 --> 00:02:04.896
And now we're heading
back another 37 minutes,

00:02:04.896 --> 00:02:06.985
so we can actually go to where the hell

00:02:06.985 --> 00:02:08.262
we were supposed to go.

00:02:08.262 --> 00:02:10.435
Oh, hey, welcome to Park City,

00:02:10.435 --> 00:02:12.169
where Carmichael and I are gonna go out,

00:02:12.169 --> 00:02:13.424
show you the sights and sounds.

00:02:13.424 --> 00:02:15.660
We've never been here either,
the first thing that we found,

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:18.204
people are super nice here.

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:21.701
So much so, that for every
person who doesn't say hi to us,

00:02:21.701 --> 00:02:24.365
I will make a snow angel in their honor.

00:02:24.365 --> 00:02:26.133
Can you imagine if you tried to say hi

00:02:26.133 --> 00:02:27.889
to everybody that you
passed in Los Angeles,

00:02:27.889 --> 00:02:29.449
how many snow angels you'd have to do?

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:34.371
To do a smog angel, you just
stand there and you do this.

00:02:34.371 --> 00:02:35.204
Let's see.

00:02:36.873 --> 00:02:38.215
(buzzer)

00:02:38.215 --> 00:02:39.778
(laughing)

00:02:39.778 --> 00:02:40.668
Does that one count?

00:02:40.668 --> 00:02:42.782
Dear guy in the green
jacket with the ski mask on

00:02:42.782 --> 00:02:45.801
that didn't say hi to
me when I said hello,

00:02:45.801 --> 00:02:49.356
may this snow angel enhance
your life, watch over you,

00:02:49.356 --> 00:02:52.023
and bring you general happiness.

00:02:53.014 --> 00:02:54.347
Oh, that's cold.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:03.018
Oh man, I better really be
more enthusiastic about this.

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:05.780
I really don't wanna do this all day.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:08.570
Hi there.

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:09.664
- [Woman] Hi.

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:11.731
- [Jack] How's it going?

00:03:11.731 --> 00:03:13.124
(buzzer)

00:03:13.124 --> 00:03:15.207
(groans)

00:03:16.633 --> 00:03:17.466
No!

00:03:18.388 --> 00:03:19.221
Fuck!

00:03:20.875 --> 00:03:24.022
Guy with the pornstache,
I am partially to blame.

00:03:24.022 --> 00:03:26.189
I should have committed to you more.

00:03:26.189 --> 00:03:28.272
Oh, this one's the worst.

00:03:29.306 --> 00:03:32.056
(playfully sobs)

00:03:34.746 --> 00:03:38.289
And that, my friends, is
a lesson about commitment.

00:03:38.289 --> 00:03:41.489
No, I think, I'm pretty sure
we're going the right way.

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:43.898
Carmichael and I are
going to the brand panel,

00:03:44.133 --> 00:03:45.962
where we're gonna speak.

00:03:45.962 --> 00:03:47.545
It starts at 11, it's 10:00 now,

00:03:47.545 --> 00:03:48.417
so we're gonna get there,

00:03:48.417 --> 00:03:51.470
do a half hour of meeting,
greeting, shaking hands.

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:52.923
There's gonna be a lot of words used,

00:03:52.923 --> 00:03:55.340
like influencer, and tune-in,

00:03:56.398 --> 00:03:58.937
and upselling, and downselling.

00:03:58.937 --> 00:04:02.417
Thank you so much for putting
all the comments in the video.

00:04:02.417 --> 00:04:04.576
Carmichael was just looking
through them very thoroughly.

00:04:04.576 --> 00:04:05.987
As soon as I get there,

00:04:05.987 --> 00:04:07.885
I will be frantically
scrolling through my phone,

00:04:07.885 --> 00:04:10.127
also reading Carmichael's executive notes

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:13.563
on what the general themes have been.

00:04:14.989 --> 00:04:16.789
Hope I'm going the right way.

00:04:17.433 --> 00:04:20.853
- [Carmichael] (laughing) Keep going.

00:04:20.853 --> 00:04:22.936
(laughs)

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:26.522
- That's a Croatian flag,
those are my people.

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:27.950
That conversation that I had back there,

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:31.584
that girl goes, "Hey, are you lost?"

00:04:31.873 --> 00:04:33.943
You want to get Minnesota-nice treatment,

00:04:33.943 --> 00:04:36.089
you have to be able to speak
with a Minnesota accent.

00:04:36.089 --> 00:04:38.889
For example, "Oh yeah,
I think, I mean, hey,

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:40.100
"I couldn't tell you one way or the other,

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:41.557
"I just know we're trying
to get to Main Street."

00:04:41.897 --> 00:04:44.834
- [Man] Yeah, if you walk up this road

00:04:44.834 --> 00:04:46.945
until you get to Heber and take
a left, it's just one block,

00:04:46.945 --> 00:04:49.151
this eventually runs
parallel to Main Street.

00:04:49.151 --> 00:04:49.984
- Oh, perfect.

00:04:49.984 --> 00:04:50.865
- [Man] Yeah, you're just
like a minute or two.

00:04:50.865 --> 00:04:52.026
- Thanks.

00:04:52.026 --> 00:04:52.859
Hey there.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:55.140
Hi.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:59.590
Hey there, how are you guys?

00:04:59.829 --> 00:05:01.236
Hey there.

00:05:01.236 --> 00:05:02.095
- [Man] Hi, how are you?

00:05:02.095 --> 00:05:03.196
- How's it going?

00:05:03.196 --> 00:05:04.169
Hi.

00:05:04.169 --> 00:05:06.252
(buzzer)

00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:07.966
Burned.

00:05:13.355 --> 00:05:15.588
(buzzer)

00:05:15.588 --> 00:05:17.671
(grunts)

00:05:23.560 --> 00:05:25.660
We are here, okay.

00:05:27.985 --> 00:05:30.174
Where do we park?

00:05:30.174 --> 00:05:33.294
So weird, it doesn't
look like anyone's here.

00:05:37.925 --> 00:05:40.358
Looks like there's plenty of parking here.

00:05:40.358 --> 00:05:42.649
Dude, soft snow is the worst.

00:05:42.649 --> 00:05:43.591
Hi, my name's Jake Watson.

00:05:43.591 --> 00:05:45.561
I'm a co-creative director
of Corridor Digital.

00:05:45.561 --> 00:05:46.589
We're a digital entertainment studio,

00:05:46.589 --> 00:05:49.057
specializing in video
game-inspired narrative content,

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:50.783
tech experiments, and vlogging.

00:05:50.783 --> 00:05:52.727
We have two YouTube channels
with a subscriber base

00:05:52.727 --> 00:05:54.075
of around 5 million.

00:05:54.075 --> 00:05:55.743
We have content on Hulu.

00:05:55.743 --> 00:05:57.587
We specialize in,

00:05:57.587 --> 00:06:01.489
we specialize in narrative
video game-inspired content,

00:06:01.489 --> 00:06:03.084
tech experiments, and blogging.

00:06:03.084 --> 00:06:05.033
We have two YouTube channels
with a combined subscribership

00:06:05.033 --> 00:06:07.130
of 5 million people.

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:09.030
600 million video views.

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:13.197
We have content on Amazon Prime,
Hulu, YouTube, YouTube Red.

00:06:14.244 --> 00:06:16.550
Go90, Facebook, Instagram.

00:06:16.550 --> 00:06:18.233
And I'm also a licensed
entertainment lawyer

00:06:18.233 --> 00:06:19.626
in the state of California.

00:06:19.626 --> 00:06:20.459
Thanks.

00:06:23.595 --> 00:06:25.426
- [Woman] It's snowing, man.

00:06:25.426 --> 00:06:26.759
- I know, right?

00:06:30.302 --> 00:06:31.716
Oh, man.

00:06:31.716 --> 00:06:34.216
We need to go buy some gloves.

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:37.780
(buzzer)

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:39.391
- [Carmichael] Did you get the bus driver?

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:40.720
- I didn't get the wave.

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:42.000
(laughs)

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:48.610
- [Carmichael] You're doing great, Jake.

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:51.981
- Harry, your hands are freezing!

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:53.986
It's gonna kill me, but I'm gonna do it.

00:06:53.986 --> 00:06:54.813
Hey, how's it going?

00:06:54.820 --> 00:06:55.792
- [Man] Good, how are you?

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:56.633
- Good.

00:06:59.279 --> 00:07:00.502
Hey guys, how ya doing? Doing good?

00:07:00.502 --> 00:07:01.448
- [Woman] Great!

00:07:01.448 --> 00:07:02.448
- All right.

00:07:07.175 --> 00:07:08.514
Hey, man.

00:07:08.514 --> 00:07:10.272
(buzzer)

00:07:10.272 --> 00:07:12.824
Dude, he looked but he stiffed me.

00:07:12.824 --> 00:07:14.124
That counts, that counts.

00:07:14.124 --> 00:07:15.502
All right, how's it going?

00:07:15.502 --> 00:07:16.302
- [Man] Good.

00:07:17.151 --> 00:07:18.688
- That guys knows what's up.

00:07:18.688 --> 00:07:19.771
- [Woman] Hi.

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:26.913
- Howdy.

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:27.440
(buzzer)

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:28.273
Damn.

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:32.200
Just when I was getting started here.

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:33.790
Hello.

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:34.863
- [Woman] Hi.

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:40.876
- All right, so after just
a little bit of doing this,

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:42.674
I think I understand what
PewDiePie and other people

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:45.679
are saying when they say that
there's forced positivity

00:07:45.907 --> 00:07:46.981
on YouTube.

00:07:46.981 --> 00:07:48.661
This is tough.

00:07:49.299 --> 00:07:51.056
You can't just go out there and, like,

00:07:51.056 --> 00:07:53.100
decide that you're gonna be emotional

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:54.599
however you're gonna be.

00:07:54.599 --> 00:07:56.322
You gotta actually put forth the effort.

00:07:56.322 --> 00:07:57.471
And it's good work, too.

00:07:57.471 --> 00:07:59.189
I think we're doing good work here.

00:07:59.189 --> 00:08:00.563
Hey, how's it going?

00:08:00.563 --> 00:08:01.063
(buzzer)

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:02.343
How's it going?

00:08:02.343 --> 00:08:03.493
- [Woman] It's going good.

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:04.533
- It's pretty good.

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:05.653
This is for the people of Park City.

00:08:05.848 --> 00:08:07.503
I think we've made the world a little bit

00:08:07.503 --> 00:08:08.739
of a better place today.

00:08:08.739 --> 00:08:10.117
I don't wanna brag but,
you know, there's a lot

00:08:10.117 --> 00:08:11.504
of more positive energy out there

00:08:11.504 --> 00:08:12.721
now that we've done our part.

00:08:12.721 --> 00:08:13.956
And I think that those people,

00:08:13.956 --> 00:08:15.657
those lonely hearts out
there that couldn't find it

00:08:15.657 --> 00:08:16.794
to say hello,

00:08:16.794 --> 00:08:18.612
I think next time they're gonna say hello.

00:08:18.612 --> 00:08:20.446
Anyways I just wanna thank
the good people of Park City.

00:08:20.446 --> 00:08:22.542
Couldn't have done it without you guys.

00:08:22.542 --> 00:08:25.305
Oh, and all you cold-hearted Angelenos

00:08:25.305 --> 00:08:26.185
that have come out here.

00:08:30.186 --> 00:08:31.601
(applause)

00:08:31.601 --> 00:08:33.329
Replication of an IP, like,

00:08:33.329 --> 00:08:35.530
if Marvel's got $300 million to go out

00:08:35.540 --> 00:08:38.572
and make Iron Man 10,
we're not gonna go out

00:08:38.572 --> 00:08:42.067
and try to make a scene from Iron Man 10.

00:08:42.067 --> 00:08:43.397
- At the end of the day,

00:08:43.397 --> 00:08:44.796
you guys, I think, are still in the battle

00:08:44.796 --> 00:08:46.838
to try to get your thing
to bubble up to the top

00:08:46.838 --> 00:08:48.431
and be the thing that everybody likes.

00:08:48.431 --> 00:08:50.100
Occasionally, there'll be ones that hits,

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:51.874
but you can't really
build a business around,

00:08:51.874 --> 00:08:53.944
you know, how many shows
have been on Vimeo?

00:08:53.944 --> 00:08:55.999
And one of them got
picked up to go to HBO.

00:08:55.999 --> 00:08:59.803
And so, for me, just purely
being the old school guy,

00:08:59.803 --> 00:09:02.057
like at some point, somebody
should get their money back,

00:09:02.057 --> 00:09:03.026
right?

00:09:03.026 --> 00:09:04.256
That's not a good proposition.

00:09:04.256 --> 00:09:05.773
So what I'm looking for on my side

00:09:05.773 --> 00:09:06.992
is the guy on your side to say,

00:09:06.992 --> 00:09:09.352
"Here's how I can make sure
you get your money back."

00:09:09.352 --> 00:09:12.803
- That didn't exist five years ago,

00:09:12.803 --> 00:09:15.694
you didn't make digital series.

00:09:15.694 --> 00:09:18.452
And we're still sort of figuring that out.

00:09:18.452 --> 00:09:20.245
But the more and more we do it,

00:09:20.245 --> 00:09:23.078
the closer and closer we
get to finding out actually

00:09:23.078 --> 00:09:25.446
where that watershed moment is.

00:09:25.446 --> 00:09:27.694
It's coming in the next year to two years.

00:09:27.694 --> 00:09:29.832
There's really gonna be a consistent model

00:09:29.832 --> 00:09:32.680
for digital series that's
gonna live off of that.

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:35.778
And now, Carmichael and
I have two more nights

00:09:35.778 --> 00:09:39.608
where we don't know
where we're gonna stay.

00:09:39.608 --> 00:09:42.608
(playful screaming)

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:51.600
- [Carmichael] She's
getting double-teamed!

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:54.499
(baby screeches)
- Holy!

00:09:55.829 --> 00:09:57.313
- What's up?
- What's up?

00:09:57.313 --> 00:09:58.146
- Hey!

